  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies a hybrid gate-based quantum-classical neural network on a simulator using 8 qubits and 8 layers for two finance classification settings and MNIST. For the balanced finance sample, the QNet reports ACC/AUC of 0.68/0.72 on test data with data re-uploading versus 0.62/0.77 for the classical NNet; for the unbalanced sample, test ACC/AUC is 0.84/0.55 for QNet with data re-uploading versus 0.83/0.51 for NNet, and on MNIST the QNet reaches 0.81 test accuracy versus 0.81 for the classical baseline.",
